{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1408151-novel-recommendation-wylding-hall-by-elizabeth-hand","id":1408151,"title":"Novel recommendation: Wylding Hall by Elizabeth Hand","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-14T07:39:26-07:00","id":1408151,"title":"Novel recommendation: Wylding Hall by Elizabeth Hand","content":"I wanted to let everyone know about the most Changeling piece of fiction I've read in a long time. <b>Wylding Hall</b> by Elizabeth Hand is a novella published in 2015. It won the Shirley Jackson award for best novella that year,<br /> <br /> A brief, non-spoilery description: Decades ago, the British folk rock group Windhollow Faire released Wylding Hall, their second and final album. Now a filmmaker is interviewing the surviving members and others for a documentary about the fateful summer it was recorded, and subsequent disappearance of the band's lead singer.<br /> <br /> I found this novella to be ideal inspiration for Changeling. Some have interpreted it as a ghost story, but I saw it as a fairy tale. I cannot recommend it highly enough for fans of Changeling: the Lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3629-bibliomancer","name":"Bibliomancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T15:09:30-07:00","id":1408593,"title":"","content":"Neat, I'll check it out. ^^<br /> <br /> Spinning Silver by Naomi Novik is my most recent Changeling-esque read! It has pretty great &quot;keeping your word/importance of your word&quot; moments from a Fae perspective, and gives a believable glimpse in how the mentality of a fae race might differ from humans. It also has a character who effectively goes through a Durance.<br /> <br /> There is a Keeper-esque character, but ultimately there are of course big differences between it and the True Fae of CtL, but it is great inspiration nonetheless. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T14:23:52-07:00","id":1417915,"title":"","content":"Definitely will have a look at it! I might also recommend &quot;War of the Flowers&quot; by Tad Williams, and &quot;Faerie Tale&quot; by Raymond E Feist, for other dark fantasy involving the Fae, but with a different take.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26456-van-owen","name":"Van Owen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T17:40:06-07:00","id":1418742,"title":"","content":"I'll definitely have to check out <i>Wyldling Hall</i> when I get the chance.<br /> <br /> Another book I really like as an inspiration for <i>Changeling the Lost</i> is <i>Forgotten Gods</i> by S.B. Stewart-Laing<span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">and </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Michael J. Chernicoff. For those unaware, it's an alternate history story taking place in 1745 Scotland. A group of Scottish rebels, fearing the British will crush them, decide to call on the Fair Folk for help and the consequences of their actions.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26495-shinsoryuu","name":"Shinsoryuu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26495_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}